Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs(wayfinder): reopen MDM tail consolidation, lock a
 single-machine target

/wayfinder was asked "one step function for all MDM work, 1 seed, 1
daily work or history" -- a materially bigger ask than the state-
machine-consolidation map's ticket 02 concluded (5 MDM Pipeline
Machines stay separate, code-sharing only).

Checked the actual duplication before grilling: daily_incremental and
load_history each hand-duplicate the identical Mastering -> Infer
Relationships -> Publish -> Publish Relationships -> Reconcile ->
GoldRefresh dict entirely outside wire_mdm_tail() -- confirmed via
grep of deploy-aws-application.sh, not inference. daily_incremental's
own generator function duplicates it twice within itself. This is the
exact drift risk ticket 02's own evidence (commit 3aa92fe9) warned
about, recurring somewhere ticket 02 never touched.

Grilled the user (AskUserQuestion) on 3 real ambiguities before
charting anything, per wayfinder's "plan, don't do." Answers:
- The MDM machine is the tail and nothing else -- no head stage lives
  inside it.
- seed_universe + mdm_seed_universe merge into 1 seed machine
  (reverses ticket 04's locked "keep separate" call).
- daily_incremental and load_history stay 2 machines, not 1 -- both
  call the MDM machine instead of inlining it.

New ticket 07 records this as the locked target, explicitly revising
ticket 02 and reversing ticket 04 (both updated with pointers, not
rewritten -- historical record preserved). New ticket 08 captures the
one genuinely open follow-up: what happens to the 5 current MDM
Pipeline Machines' distinct heads (ownership parsing, silver batching,
residual-holds derivation, bronze_seed_silver_gold's separate strict-
mode branch) once the tail they each hand-duplicate becomes one shared
callee machine instead of copy-pasted states.

No code changed -- this is wayfinder planning only, one ticket
resolved (07), one new frontier ticket opened (08) per the skill's
"never resolve more than one ticket per session" rule.

